Adjacency-only residency for DiskANN (the "record split").

A DiskANN node record is [vector][nnbrs][nbrs]: 132 B of adjacency against a
260 B (uint8) or 644 B (float32) record, so adjacency is 20-51% of the record and
a 4,096 B sector read yields 132 B of graph structure -- 31x amplification.

Two facts in cached_beam_search make the split possible:
  * _nhood_cache membership ALONE decides whether a node needs a disk read; a node
    found there never enters `frontier`, so no I/O is issued for it.
  * _coord_cache is consulted only to compute an expanded node's EXACT distance.

So caching adjacency WITHOUT coordinates removes the disk read while costing only
distance precision -- which the PQ table already approximates. For SIFT10M that is
1.32 GB instead of 6.4 GB, ~5x less memory for the same elimination of reads.

Motivation: full residency was measured at 11.77x QPS (192.9 -> 2,271.0) at
bit-identical recall 0.9521, but it costs 6.4 GB. Every cheaper mechanism tried --
frequency cache selection, sector admission, in-degree ranking, BFS / greedy-
neighbour / spatial / profile-guided layout, page-native construction -- failed
because each had to SELECT a subset, and which nodes a future query touches is
unpredictable (Jaccard 0.011 between disjoint query halves). Adjacency-only
residency selects nothing: coverage is total. See
Results/layout-refutation-and-the-record-split.

WHAT THIS MEASURES: recall under PQ-only expansion. The patch does NOT add a rerank
pass, so every expanded node's distance is the PQ estimate and the final ranking is
PQ-based. That makes the measured recall a LOWER BOUND -- a deployment would rerank
the top-k by reading k full vectors (~10 reads/query), recovering precision at small
cost. The number of interest is how far the candidate set degrades without it.

Env-gated by DISKANN_ADJ_ONLY_CACHE=1; completely inert when unset, so the same
image reproduces stock behaviour. Applies to a clean tree (touches only
src/pq_flash_index.cpp; robin_map_hash_fix.patch touches include/pq_flash_index.h,
so the two do not conflict). Build from ann-suite/diskann:hashfix.

This is a TIMED-measurement image: it adds no counters or tracing.

